## 2. Testbed Domain: Multi-Vendor E-Commerce & Logistics Platform

The chosen testbed domain is a **Multi-Vendor E-Commerce, Inventory, and Reviews Platform**. This domain is ideal because it naturally encapsulates every single NoSQL design pattern and relational database edge case in software engineering.

### 2.1 Core Collections & Document Shapes

| MongoDB Collection | NoSQL Design Pattern | Relational Challenge | Target PostgreSQL Mapping |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **`users`** | 1:1 Embedding, Field Drift | Nested address objects, mixed phone types | `users` table + flattened `address_*` columns or separate `addresses` table |
| **`products`** | Polymorphism, Attribute Pattern | Variable attributes per category (Tech vs Clothing) | `products` table + `specs` as `JSONB` or category-specific tables |
| **`categories`** | Tree / Self-Referencing | Hierarchical parent-child taxonomy | `categories` table with self-referencing `parent_id` Foreign Key |
| **`orders`** | 1:N Embedding, Denormalization | Embedded line items with price snapshots | Split into `orders` (parent) and `order_items` (child) with Foreign Keys |
| **`reviews`** | Hybrid Referencing / Embedding | User references + product references + ratings | `reviews` table with compound Foreign Keys |
| **`inventory_logs`** | High-Volume Time Series | Massive rows, timestamps in mixed formats | `inventory_logs` table with partitioned timestamps and indexes |
| **`coupons`** | Complex Constraints | Validity dates, percentage/flat discounts, usage caps | `coupons` table with SQL `CHECK` constraints |

