## 3. Comprehensive Matrix of 10 Edge Cases to Test

The MongoDB testbed will be seeded with specific edge cases designed to test every layer of the migration planner:

```mermaid
classDiagram
    class UserDocument {
        +_id ObjectId/UUID
        +name String
        +email String
        +phone Int64 / String (Drift)
        +isActive Boolean / "yes" (Type Mismatch)
        +profile Object (Deep Nesting)
        +tags Array~String~ (Primitives Array)
        +createdAt ISODate / Timestamp / String
    }
    class ProductDocument {
        +_id ObjectId
        +title String
        +category String
        +price Double / Int
        +attributes Object (Polymorphic)
        +media Array~Object~ (Nested Objects)
    }
    class OrderDocument {
        +_id ObjectId
        +userId ObjectId (Referential FK)
        +items Array~OrderItem~ (1:N Embedding)
        +shippingAddress Object
        +payment Object
    }
    UserDocument --> OrderDocument : 1 to N
    ProductDocument --> OrderDocument : Referenced
```

### Detailed Edge Case Breakdown:

1. **Polymorphic Data in Single Collection:**
   * *MongoDB Reality:* Electronics documents have `{ ram: "32GB", cpu: "M3" }`, while Clothing has `{ size: "M", color: "Red", fabric: "Cotton" }`.
   * *Test Objective:* Verifies if the AI properly identifies when to store flexible attributes as PostgreSQL `JSONB` versus creating normalized child tables.

2. **Schema Drift & Type Inconsistency (Dirty Data):**
   * *MongoDB Reality:* Documents 1–500 have `phone: 9876543210` (Integer); Documents 501–1500 have `phone: "+91-98765-43210"` (String); Documents 1501–2000 have `phone: null`.
   * *Test Objective:* Verifies the ETL engine's type-sanitization pipeline safely coerces or converts types without terminating the entire migration batch.

3. **Embedded 1:N Arrays (The Table Splitter):**
   * *MongoDB Reality:* `orders.items` is an array of 1 to 20 objects inside each order document.
   * *Test Objective:* Verifies the planner splits this collection into two tables (`orders` and `order_items`), generating synthetic UUID/Serial primary keys and foreign keys for the child table.

4. **Primitive Arrays vs. Object Arrays:**
   * *MongoDB Reality:* `products.tags = ["electronics", "laptop", "sale"]` (array of strings) vs. `products.variants = [{ sku: "A1", price: 10 }]` (array of objects).
   * *Test Objective:* Verifies the system maps primitive arrays to PostgreSQL native arrays (`TEXT[]`) and object arrays to normalized relational tables.

5. **Date and Timestamp Format Diversity:**
   * *MongoDB Reality:* Mixed dates stored as BSON `ISODate`, Unix timestamps (numeric `1718000000`), and ISO-8601 strings (`"2026-08-15T00:00:00Z"`).
   * *Test Objective:* Verifies that date normalization parsers convert all variations into PostgreSQL `TIMESTAMPTZ`.

6. **Deep Nested Object Paths (Multi-Level Hierarchy):**
   * *MongoDB Reality:* `{ user: { meta: { billing: { address: { coordinates: { lat: 19.07, lng: 72.87 } } } } } }`.
   * *Test Objective:* Verifies path flattening (`user_meta_billing_address_lat`) or GeoJSON point conversion (`POINT(72.87, 19.07)`).

7. **Null vs. Undefined vs. Missing Fields:**
   * *MongoDB Reality:* Document A has `{ discount: 0 }`, Document B has `{ discount: null }`, Document C omits the `discount` field entirely.
   * *Test Objective:* Verifies nullable SQL column definitions and avoids SQL `NOT NULL` constraint violations.

8. **Large Document Payloads & Field Sizes:**
   * *MongoDB Reality:* High-resolution product descriptions containing 50KB+ of HTML/text or large embedded event logs.
   * *Test Objective:* Verifies PostgreSQL data types (`TEXT` vs `VARCHAR(255)`) and streaming cursor memory consumption under 25MB RAM.

9. **Topological Order & Foreign Key Dependencies:**
   * *MongoDB Reality:* Orders reference `userId` and `productId`. Categories reference parent `categoryId`.
   * *Test Objective:* Verifies the migration planner analyzes the Dependency Graph and creates/populates tables in topological order (`categories` $\rightarrow$ `users` $\rightarrow$ `products` $\rightarrow$ `orders` $\rightarrow$ `order_items`).

10. **Index Migration & Full-Text Search:**
    * *MongoDB Reality:* Compound indexes on `{ category: 1, price: -1 }` and text search indexes on `{ title: "text", description: "text" }`.
    * *Test Objective:* Verifies automatic translation into PostgreSQL B-Tree and GIN `to_tsvector` full-text search indexes.

